      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Devastation [zone=339]\n**Who:**\n- Oathmir the Outcast [npc=20377]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 70\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Loot\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 01:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Runed Silver Box [item=48704]\n- Sealed Runed Silver Box [item=48705]\n- Vial of Corrupted Blood [item=48373]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Razorthorn: Samples of Corruption [zone=382]\n- Sverag, Stronghold of Rage [zone=341]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- a crumbling chest [npc=21459]\n- a shadow of rage [npc=21302]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Access to the Theater of Blood/Plane of Music [quest=3444]\n- Become the Vessel (Razorthorn Access) [quest=3428]\n- PoR Level 70 Spell #1: The Key To The Past [quest=3390]\n- PoR Level 70 Spell #2: The Burning Prince [quest=3391]\n- Preparing Your New Skins [quest=3429]\n- Saga Skins [quest=3427]\n- Skylance: The Laboratory [quest=3420]\n- Skylance: The Library [quest=3366]\n- Skylance: The Oubliette [quest=3419]\n**Era:** | !Prophecy of Ro\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Apr 9 05:20:25 2006\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This task can only be obtained by someone who has completed the Razorthorn access task \" **Become the Vessel** [quest=3428]\"._\n_It begins with Oathmir the Outcast at the zone-in of The Devastation._\nYou say, 'Hail, Oathmir the Outcast'\nOathmir the Outcast looks you up and down, taking in your weapons and instinctively gauging your ability. He replies in a somber tone. 'Hello. You are different than the rest of us here. You have not come here from the wall. You have somehow come straight from the world.' The outcast slowly shakes his head. 'You should leave this place before its nature becomes your own. I don't believe that you want to become part of the cycle here. Anger released upon others returns tenfold to the giver, they say. I have been in [the wall] and I will go there again, though each time it takes me longer to return, longer to fight my way back. I have been cast from the cycle. I no longer have enough rage in my heart. I [feel disconnected] from Her and without my rage and my desire I have nothing.'\nYou say, 'Why do you feel disconnected?'\nOathmir the Outcast says 'I am lost, but I feel that I have a purpose here. It is difficult to explain to someone that has never been part of the cycle what it is like to be taken from it. I have lost all rage and have been left with emptiness. I no longer feel the desire to be with Her in the tower. I felt the rage leaving me slowly from the moment I was chosen as Vessel. She touched me then, instilling me with her rage, but it did not feel right to me. It was somehow tainted, impure. I could not accept it and the moment I rejected her rage all of my rage started to flow away from me. Something is very wrong with our goddess. Her rage is no longer pure, though it may be my own heart that is corrupt. Perhaps you [can find] out what has happened. Perhaps you can get into the tower and find out what has gone wrong.'\nYou say, 'I can find out.'\nOathmir the Outcast says 'Take this chest to store any clues you may find. Return to me should you [need another].'\n_You are handed a Runed Silver Box and offered the choice of doing the task on normal or hard setting. NOTE: Loot tables are reportedly shared between hard mode and normal mode._\nYou have been assigned the task 'Samples of Corruption'.\nThe corruption spreading through the tower has affected some of the residents more than others. I would have you collect the blood of the most corrupt residents in the tower. Once you have filled the box wirg samples, return them to me so I might study them.\n\n---\n\nEnter Razorthorn, Tower of Sullon Zek 0/1 (Sverag, Stronghold of Rage)\n_This is entered through a door in the center of Sverag, the Stronghold of Rage._\nLoot 10 vials of corrupted blood 0/10 (Razorthorn, Tower of Sullon Zek)\n_These can drop off any mob in the zone. Note: Mobs hit for a max ~1,200 and respawn. Respawns don't drop the Vials. Only originally spawned mobs will drop the item._\n_Every so often, \"a shadow of rage\" spawns and attacks the group, charming a group member as it does so. The charm lasts 2.5 minutes (or will be broken sooner if the shadow dies beforehand)._\nSeal the blood vials samples in the chest 0/1 (ALL)\n_Combine the blood vials in the Runed Silver Box to craft a Sealed Runed Silver Box._\nReturn the sealed chest to Oathmir 0/1 (The Devastation)\n_Upon handing in the sealed box:_\nYou have done well. It will take me some time to examine these, but I can only hope they will hold some answers for the dilemmas we face.\n_\"a crumbling chest\" spawns with one item of loot:_\nBlackened Fury Forged Pauldron\nPitted Blade of the Fallen Lord\nRage-Scarred Gorget\n_Also, there are random rare zonewide drops in this task:_\nFlawless Pearl of Tranquility\nGlyphed Stone of Animosity\nRuned Stone of Wrath\n_NOTE: Loot tables are reportedly shared between hard mode and normal mode._\n\n---\n\n**Progression**\n_At any time after the task is complete you are able to hand Oathmir the Silent Harmonic Chime that is obtained after completing the three Skylance Tasks._\nOathmir the Outcast takes the tiny charm in his huge hands. He spins it slightly as it dangles from his thick fingers, staring at it intently.\n\"Yes, I think I understand. This is tuned to a place, but that place is not as I expected, much like my experience with Her. I think I can change this, make it more receptive to unexpected versions of the original place.\"\nHe takes the pieces of the chime individually and rolls them between thumb and forefinger. Each time he does there is a loud and visible explosion and a creaking sound. These explosions are contained within the thick calluses of the giant's finger pads. Oathmir hums throughout, a deep sound like distant earthquakes. Once he has done this with each he hands the chime back to you.\n\"That might work for you, though I'm afraid I had to crush the magic that was there before to make the adjustment\".\n_Oathmir gives you a Twisted Chime._\n**Submitted by:** Lias Roxx, Defiant, Zek\n- Blackened Fury Forged Pauldron [item=48374]\n- Flawless Pearl of Tranquility [item=51414]\n- Glyphed Stone of Animosity [item=50684]\n- Pitted Blade of the Fallen Lord [item=48945]\n- Rage-Scarred Gorget [item=48375]\n- Runed Stone of Wrath [item=50734]",
