      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Devastation [zone=339]\n**What:**\n- Decorated Wurine Hide [item=48498]\n- Etched Drachnid Carapace [item=48583]\n- Inked Evil Eye Hide [item=48582]\n- Mummified Pigmented Skin [item=48581]\n- Patch of Dyed Kobold Fur [item=48559]\n- Scarred Bolvirk Skin [item=48508]\n- Scarred and Tattooed Skin [item=48586]\n- Tattooed Shiliskin Skin [item=48585]\n- Torn and Tattooed Orc Flesh [item=48580]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Time:** | Unlimited\n**Level:** | 70\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Spell\n**Quest Items:**\n- Berserker Lore Skin Translation [item=48499]\n- Bolvirk Lore Skin Translation [item=48588]\n- Drachnid Lore Skin Translation [item=48589]\n- Evil Eye Lore Skin Translation [item=48590]\n- Kobold Lore Skin Translation [item=48591]\n- Orc Lore Skin Translation [item=48592]\n- Saga Skin Translations Vol. 1 [item=48596]\n- Saga Skin Translations Vol. 2 [item=48597]\n- Shiliskin Lore Skin Translation [item=48593]\n- Undead Lore Skin Translation [item=48594]\n- Wurine Lore Skin Translation [item=48595]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Razorthorn, Tower of Sullon Zek [zone=342]\n- Sverag, Stronghold of Rage [zone=341]\n- The Plane of Knowledge [zone=158]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Grand Librarian Maelin [npc=10635]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Become the Vessel (Razorthorn Access) [quest=3428]\n- Preparing Your New Skins [quest=3429]\n**Era:** | !Prophecy of Ro\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Apr 21 06:55:30 2006\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | _This task is the first of three tasks for Razorthorn access._\n_This task is assigned to you when you loot a Lore No Drop skin in The Devastation. The task requires looting a total of nine such skins, and once you have the task you will get credit for looting skins that drop in Sverag or Razorthorn instances._\nYou have discovered some very interesting patterns on the skin of warriors in the Plane of Rage. Gather more information by collecting a variety of these skins.\nFind more of these strangely patterned skins 0/1 ALL\n_Loot Scarred Bolvirk Skin off Bolvirk (giant)_\nFind more of these strangely patterned skins 0/1 ALL\n_Loot Mummified Pigmented Skin off Undead or Horse._\nFind more of these strangely patterned skins 0/1 ALL\n_Loot Patch of Dyed Kobold Fur off Kobold._\nFind more of these strangely patterned skins 0/1 ALL\n_Loot Torn and Tattooed Orc Flesh off Orc._\nFind more of these strangely patterned skins 0/1 ALL\n_Loot Inked Evil Eye Hide off Evil Eye._\nFind more of these strangely patterned skins 0/1 ALL\n_Loot Decorated Wurine Hide off Werewolf._\nFind more of these strangely patterned skins 0/1 ALL\n_Loot Etched Drachnid Carapace off Drachnid._\nFind more of these strangely patterned skins 0/1 ALL\n_Loot Tattooed Shiliskin Skin off Shiliskin._\nFind more of these strangely patterned skins 0/1 ALL\n_Loot Scarred and Tattooed Skin off Berserker (Barbarian, Vah Shir, Troll)._\n_Hunt level 73 mobs (red con to level 70) for the best drop rate. Some will drop two. Yellow con mobs will occasionally drop skins, but not often._\nFind someone to translate the patterns on the Bolvirk skin 0/1 ALL\n_Hand Scarred Bolvirk Skin to Grand Librarian Maelin_\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'I've never seen anything like it before. The being that you took this skin from obviously belongs to a culture that uses scarring and tattooing to represent rank of some sort. Most likely a scar or tattoo is earned in battle or when coming of age. The more scars the more power the creature would have in their society. But there is another layer of meaning here. There is a section here that appears to be written in a form of the giant language, then disguised with a laughably simple code. It appears to be a fragment of some sort of legend. . . Here, let me write it down for you.'\n_He hands you the Scarred Bolvirk Skin and Bolvirk Lore Skin Translation._\nFind someone to translate the patterns on the Undead skin. 0/1 ALL\n_Hand Mummified Pigmented Skin to Grand Librarian Maelin._\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'Well, this is strange. This flesh has obviously been preserved using necromancy. But the inking that has been done to it is relatively fresh, done after the preservation and after dead. This is hard for me to translate normally, but I have some special tricks for understanding magical writing. I'll write this down for you, but the general idea here is that it talks of a ritual of passage, something about becoming full. I guess I never really understood the undead, perhaps you can make sense of it.'\n_He hands you the Mummified Pigmented Skin and Undead Lore Skin Translation._\nFind someone to translate the patterns on the Kobold fur. 0/1 ALL\n_Hand Patch of Dyed Kobold Fur to Grand Librarian Maelin._\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'What beautiful patterns! They look like decorations, at least at first glance. But I have a keen eye for art and an even keener one for patterns. There's a language in there, something like Kobold. It's sort of a pictorial description of, well, of a story about a powerful Kobold who became a god. It also talks about another god, a female. Here's a transcription, as best as I can make it. It's by no means complete, but with more information it might mean something.'\n_He hands you the Patch of Dyed Kobold Fur and Kobold Lore Skin Translation._\nFind someone to translate the patterns on the Orc skin. 0/1 ALL\n_Hand Torn and Tattooed Orc Flesh to Grand Librarian Maelin._\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'I've always known that orcs liked to paint themselves at times of war, but I've never seen this. These markings are permanent and appear to be very, very old. I'm very familiar with orcish languages, but I've never seen this one. It appears to be a combination of several modern and ancient versions of orcish. The combination makes it very hard to read, but it seems as though it is a history of something called a vessel. I've written it down for you, but you'll need more information to make sense out of it.'\n_He hands you the Torn and Tattooed Orc Flesh and Orc Lore Skin Translation._\nFind someone to translate the patterns on the Evil eye 0/1 ALL\n_Hand Inked Evil Eye Hide to Grand Librarian Maelin._\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'Well, this is very odd indeed. You say that this is the skin from an Evil Eye? I have never heard of those creatures cutting designs into themselves or each other, but that's exactly what this appears to be. Even more surprising is the fact that this appears to be more than just a result of combat, it seems to be a code of some sort. The eyes are rather bright, and this makes it easier for me to understand what this code means, there's a logic behind it. It seems to be a path or method to achieve power in a place it calls Rage. There are a lot of details missing, of course, but here is my translation of the information encoded onto this bit of skin.'\n_He hands you the Inked Evil Eye Hide and Evil Eye Lore Skin Translation._\nFind someone to translate the patterns on the Wurine fur. 0/1 ALL\n_Hand Decorated Wurine Hide to Grand Librarian Maelin._\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'This is a fantastic pelt. It's scarred and bloody, sure, but look at it! Under the blood and fur there is a pattern scratched into the skin. It's not just an animal scratching at fleas, it's an actual language of sort. Very primitive and so very hard for me to understand, but I can make some sense of it. The text is by no means complete, but I see references to rage and anger and the perfecting of those emotions. Something about power and completeness being linked to such perfection. I guess it makes sense that a creature with such emotions would seek to the perfect form. Here, I've made some notes about what's written here. With enough information perhaps it will make some sense.'\n_He hands you the Decorated Wurine Hide and Wurine Lore Skin Translation._\nFind someone to translate the patterns on the Drachnid carapace. 0/1 ALL\n_Hand Etched Drachnid Carapace to Grand Librarian Maelin._\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'Well, isn't this unpleasant! Spiders give me the creeps, you know. Huge sentient spiders. . . well it makes me dizzy to think of it! But I am a scholar and I must overcome this and examine this thing you brought me. Yes, there are definitely markings on this. It seems to be a version of Dark Speech and therefore easy enough to understand, but there is some form of code involved. I can only assume that this is to prevent it from being read easily. Why would someone do this? From what I can read of this, it seems to be the only way that this creature could retain memory of important information. It refers to itself as a Lore Warrior and implies that there are others, not all of the same species. Very interesting. Here, this is a copy of what I can read on this, um, skin. Perhaps with enough information a more complete picture will be visible.'\n_He hands you the Etched Drachnid Carapace and Drachnid Lore Skin Translation._\nFind someone to translate the patterns on the Shiliskin skin. 0/1 ALL\n_Hand Tattooed Shiliskin Skin to Grand Librarian Maelin._\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'Well, this is not at all slimy as I would have expected! It's still a bit disgusting, though. I wonder what sort ink they used for these markings. It appears to be very long-lasting, and yet these markings have been retouched several times. I would think that markings this deep in the skin would last far longer than one lifetime. The language is incomprehensible to me, but I can understand the pictures easily enough. It seems to imply that this culture believes in a power beyond theirs and that there is a longing within them to serve that power. There is also an underlying tone that seems to suggest that they would destroy and replace that power once allowed into its service. Here, take these notes and this skin. It's a bit too creepy for me.'\n_He hands you the Tattooed Shiliskin Skin and Shiliskin Lore Skin Translation._\nFind someone to translate the patterns on the berserker skin. 0/1 ALL\n_Hand Scarred and Tattooed Skin to Grand Librarian Maelin._\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'Hmm, I'm not sure that I want to be known for my interpretation of skin art as language, but I'll see if I can make sense of it. The pigment seems familiar, like something the Northmen use. And the patterns seem similar as well. From what I understand of the iconography of that culture, this seems to be a story about Sullon Zek. Well, a very small part of the story, anyway. Most of it is missing. I wonder if the rest of the body had the story, or if it was carried in many pieces by separate people who would come together to be one book, so to speak. Here is what I can understand of the tale. Perhaps you can find enough pages to get an understanding of the whole story.'\n_He hands you the Scarred and Tattooed Skin and Berserker Lore Skin Translation._\n_Keep the returned skins for later use._\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'I see that you have a large number of translations from those saga skins. If you can bind them together into a book using a book binding and bring it back to me, I might be able to show you how to perform the rite that is described. I'm not really sure why any sane person would choose to do so, but perhaps you do.'\nCreate a book using a book binding and all nine pages. 0/1 ALL\n_Combine the nine Lore Skin Translations in a book binding (a container sold at most home cities) to make:_\n_Saga Skin Translations - vol. 1_\n_Saga Skin Translations - vol. 2_\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new!\nYour task 'Saga Skins' has been updated.\nYou have created a book that explains the strange phenomena of the so-called lore warriors in the Plane of Rage. Hold onto it and the skins you gathered, Maelin might have enough information to make use of your book. When you think you are ready for a challenge and you have gathered some friends together, give Maelin the book back and he will tell you where to start.\n_This ends the task. Despite the warning to gather some friends, it is safe to immediately hand these two Translations to Maelin to receive your class spell._\nYou have been assigned the task 'Preparing Your New Skin'.\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'Well, these are very interesting! I've learned a lot from the things you have brought me, so I wanted you to have this.'\n_Doing so will assign you the task \"Preparing your New Skin\", which has no time limit. It is the task after that (\"Becoming the Vessel\") where you will have a time limit and need to be ready with friends._\n_Class rewards:_\n_Bard - Spell: Arcane Aria_\n_Beastlord - Skill: Rake_\n_Berserker - Skill: Bloodthirst_\n_Cleric - Spell: Elixir of Divinity_\n_Druid - Spell: Barkspur_\n_Enchanter - Spell: Ward of Bedazzlement_\n_Magician - Spell: Spear of Ro_\n_Monk - Skill: Heel of Kanji_\n_Necromancer - Spell: Grave Pact_\n_Paladin - Spell: Ward of Tunare_\n_Ranger - Spell: Scorched Earth_\n_Rogue - Skill: Razorarc_\n_Shadowknight - Spell: Theft of Agony_\n_Shaman - Spell: Nectar of Pain_\n_Warrior - Skill: Mock_\n_Wizard - Spell: Ice Block_\n**Submitted by:** Lias Roxx, Defiant, Zek\n- Skill: Bloodthirst [item=48658]\n- Skill: Heel of Kanji [item=48650]\n- Skill: Mock [item=48638]\n- Skill: Razorarc [item=48646]\n- Spell: Arcane Aria [item=48629]\n- Spell: Barkspur [item=48631]\n- Spell: Elixir of Divinity [item=48587]\n- Spell: Grave Pact [item=48630]\n- Spell: Ice Block [item=48628]\n- Spell: Nectar of Pain [item=47712]\n- Spell: Scorched Earth [item=48626]\n- Spell: Spear of Ro [item=48859]\n- Spell: Theft of Agony [item=48584]\n- Spell: Ward of Bedazzlement [item=48639]\n- Spell: Ward of Tunare [item=48632]\n- Tome of Rake [item=47705]",
